Problem: Merge Sorted Array (LC 88)

Pattern: Two Pointers (Merge from End)

Approach:

1. Initialize:

   * i = m - 1 (last valid element of nums1)
   * j = n - 1 (last element of nums2)
   * k = m + n - 1 (last position of nums1)
2. Compare `nums1[i]` and `nums2[j]`.
3. Place the larger element at `nums1[k]`.
4. Move the corresponding pointer (`i` or `j`) and decrement `k`.
5. Repeat until either array is exhausted.
6. If elements remain in `nums2`, copy them into `nums1`.
7. Return (the array is modified in-place).

Time Complexity: O(m + n)

Space Complexity: O(1)
